From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: cdns-dphy: preserve the calibration wait time when starting the state machine

cdns_dphy_power_on() started the TX state machine by writing
DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN | DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN over the whole DPHY_CMN_SSM
register, which zeroes the calibration wait time field in bits 8..1.
Measured on Astrial H15: DPHY_CMN_SSM reads 0x00000201 after power_on,
bits 8..1 at zero.

Mainline reads the register and keeps DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME,
GENMASK(8, 1), when setting the two enable bits. Do the same.

Preserving a field instead of overwriting it cannot make things worse:
if its reset value is zero nothing changes, if it is not, we stop
destroying it. It sits in the PHY start-up path, where the unexplained
262 ms lane wait on the first modeset after boot also sits.

Mainline also waits for PLL lock and O_CMN_READY right after this write.
Those waits are not backported: in mainline they are callbacks that exist
only in j721e_dphy_ops, use registers of the TI J721E wrapper, and are
no-ops for the reference ops this integration uses.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 
 #define DPHY_CMN_SSM			DPHY_PMA_CMN(0x20)
 #define DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN			BIT(0)
+#define DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME	GENMASK(8, 1)
 #define DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN		BIT(9)
 
 #define DPHY_CMN_PWM			DPHY_PMA_CMN(0x40)
@@ -323,6 +324,7 @@
 static int cdns_dphy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 {
 	struct cdns_dphy *dphy = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	u32 reg;
 
 	if (!dphy->is_configured || dphy->is_powered)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -332,7 +334,8 @@
 	clk_prepare_enable(dphy->esc_clk);
 
 	/* Start TX state machine. */
-	writel(DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN | DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN,
+	reg = readl(dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
+	writel((reg & DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME) | DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN | DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN,
 	       dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
 
 	dphy->is_powered = true;
